23
00:01:55,420 --> 00:02:00,320
But just for some clarity, when you're charting the course, where we are as a church and where we're headed,

24
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:10,140
man, so far, the process of this merge has gone so much more seamlessly and beautifully than any of us could have ever imagined.

25
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:14,980
We believed it, we thought that it was going to be good, but just know that difficulty comes.

26
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:20,500
And so we've been calling it, a lot of us behind the scenes have been calling it the honeymoon phase, right?

27
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,720
Like, things are good.

28
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:29,480
But as you learn to live together, those of you that are married know that as you learn to live together,

29
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:34,080
things come up that you weren't fully prepared for or didn't see coming.

30
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:40,880
And so this new stage in our church merger, we've been kind of using this language, learning to live together.

31
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:48,240
And I remember when Melissa and I got married, I was living in an apartment for a couple of months in my hometown.

32
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,120
I had a full-time job.

33
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:50,800
I had a life.

34
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,500
I had a pattern.

35
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,120
I had things that I did.

36
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:59,000
And one of the worst things that I did in the first year of marriage was I kind of just, like, kept doing life.

37
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,980
And she moved into my apartment and participated in my schedule.

38
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,440
And it was like, I didn't even realize what I was doing.

39
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:10,420
But what I was doing is I was inviting us to start this new life together.

40
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:13,060
But in reality, I was asking her to just do my stuff.

41
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:19,180
