Like, it feels good right now, but it is going to catch up to me very, very quickly.

72
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:19,360
And so what I don't want for us as a church is I don't want us to just get out of the gate at this grazing, fast pace where things feel great, like we're doing awesome things for the kingdom, but we're not really taking care of what we need to take care of.

73
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:31,100
And so my fear is that if you get out of the gate too fast, we might have some initial success, but that might get in the way of our long-term success.

74
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:39,540
And my hope and my prayer, and I know many of our hopes and prayers, is that this church should be a kingdom outpost in this community for a long time to come.

75
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:43,740
And so if we're going to do that, we need to move as fast as it's wise.

76
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:48,300
And for many of you, as fast as it's wise, it's going to feel way too slow.

77
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:52,880
And for many of you, as fast as it's wise, it's going to feel way too fast.

78
00:05:53,660 --> 00:06:00,200
And so my hope and my prayer is that we would kind of figure that pace out together as a leadership to start that course.

79
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:10,780
One thing that I want to do over the next couple of weeks when that gets back is just give us a 12-month calendar of when we're going to start to really focus on certain things like small groups and outreach and discipleship strategies.

80
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:20,580
And all of the things that I know you guys are eager to get started on, just keep pacing with us if we seek to start a course that is as fast as it's wise.

81
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:21,240
Is that fair?

82
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,440
All right.

